#### Pitfall 6: **Stale Cursors After Schema Changes**

**Problem:**
```text
1. Client receives cursor: {"lastId":12345,"sortBy":"submittedDate"}
2. API deployment changes sort field name: submittedDate → submissionDate
3. Client uses old cursor
4. API fails to decode cursor or applies wrong filter
```

**Solution:**
```csharp
// Version cursors to handle schema evolution
public class CursorToken
{
    public int Version { get; set; } = 1; // Increment on breaking changes
}

// Validate version
if (cursorToken.Version != _currentCursorVersion)
{
    return BadRequest("Cursor version mismatch. Please start a new request.");
}

// Or: Support multiple cursor versions with migration logic
var decodedData = cursorToken.Version switch
{
    1 => MigrateV1ToV2(cursorToken),
    2 => cursorToken, // Current version
    _ => throw new InvalidOperationException("Unsupported cursor version")
};
```

